Subject: [MONA] Treat explicit AIR cargo slots as empty

Paper 26.1.2 can expose an explicit AIR ItemStack for an empty inventory slot.
Slimefun's CargoUtils only checked for null before calling isItemSimilar.
That path eventually called CustomItemDataService#getItemData with AIR's null
ItemMeta and aborted the whole Cargo network tick.

Apply these two guards to the MONA SlimefunCore4-2834 source before building.
The same check is required for DirtyChestMenu and vanilla Inventory targets.

--- a/src/main/java/io/github/thebusybiscuit/slimefun4/core/networks/cargo/CargoUtils.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/github/thebusybiscuit/slimefun4/core/networks/cargo/CargoUtils.java
@@ -279,4 +279,7 @@ final class CargoUtils {
-            if (itemInSlot == null) {
+            // Paper can expose an explicit AIR stack for an otherwise empty slot.
+            // Treat it exactly like null before Slimefun's metadata comparison;
+            // AIR has no ItemMeta and would otherwise make getByItem throw.
+            if (itemInSlot == null || itemInSlot.getType().isAir() || itemInSlot.getAmount() <= 0) {
                 menu.replaceExistingItem(slot, stack);
                 return null;
             }
@@ -333,4 +336,4 @@ final class CargoUtils {
-            if (itemInSlot == null) {
+            if (itemInSlot == null || itemInSlot.getType().isAir() || itemInSlot.getAmount() <= 0) {
                 inv.setItem(slot, stack);
                 return null;
             } else {
